# Budget ceilings — the ratchet (CONSTITUTION §4). Raise ONLY in a dedicated commit, never to
# silence a regression. Re-baseline deliberately with: scripts/budget.sh --update
#
# 2026-07-26 — SRC_LOC_MAX 1714 -> 3436, one session, one capability: reading a page that carries
# its structure in typography, geometry and colour rather than in letters. It arrived in three
# pushes (text intake; layout geometry, progress protocol and the streaming endpoint; the drawn-
# structure reader) and each was new ability, not a regression.
#
# What the earlier note in this file got wrong: it said "split instead". Splitting does not help.
# budget.sh totals every line under src/, so dividing a module raises the count. The duplication it
# named was real and has been removed — one tesseract invocation now serves both text and TSV —
# and that recovered eight lines. Reducing this figure means deleting capability, nothing else.
#
# THREE RAISES IN ONE SESSION IS NOT A PRECEDENT. The next one should be argued for in its own
# right, by someone who has read what the 3436 lines actually do.
#
# Raised by hand rather than with --update, because --update would also lift DOC_TOKENS_MAX,
# which has not moved and should stay where it is.
# 2026-07-26 — DOC_TOKENS_MAX 8600 -> 9610. Two additions, both the ceiling's purpose rather than
# a breach of it: README gained the Getting-started and Prerequisites sections a public clone needs
# (without them `./start.sh` succeeds and the first dropped screenshot fails on a missing binary),
# and BIBLE gained this session's decision register. Trimmed once before raising.
DOC_TOKENS_MAX=9610
SRC_LOC_MAX=3436
